WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.372
Spark is not always the right tool.

00:00:02.372 --> 00:00:08.422
A conventional database may be better for transactional workloads, frequent small updates,

00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:13.192
low-latency point lookups, and strict relational constraints.

00:00:13.192 --> 00:00:18.672
If the data fits comfortably in the database and the query workload is already efficient,

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:23.217
moving to Spark may add complexity without much benefit.

00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:30.637
Connect this idea to a retail pipeline aggregating high-volume sales data across partitions.

00:00:30.637 --> 00:00:36.382
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.382 --> 00:00:44.457
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:44.457 --> 00:00:50.617
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:56.475
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
